From Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anoane <anos@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 01:34:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] engine: FREETOKEN_MOE_STATS=1 enables the per-layer
 decode miss counters and logs them

OffloadMoeCache already accumulates per-layer active/miss/call counters on device
(lru_stats, graph-safe) behind EngineConfig.moe_collect_stats, but nothing turned
the flag on from the command line and nothing read the counters back.

- engine: FREETOKEN_MOE_STATS=1 sets cache.collect_stats before graph capture.
- scheduler: every 250 decode steps log one "[moe-stats]" JSON line with
  decode_miss_stats_per_layer() plus the offload-bank -> checkpoint-layer map
  (glm5_next.moe.offload_moe_layers), so the cumulative miss rate of every
  offloaded layer can be read from the serve log.

Used to pick the VRAM-resident layer set from data: over 2,999 greedy decode
steps on GLM-5.3-Flash the early layers miss hardest (3-6: 0.85-0.87, 7-10:
0.77-0.80, 11-16: 0.65-0.74) while 18-19 and 34 miss ~0.51-0.53; the resulting
set 3-16,23,43-44 covers 47% of all misses versus 45% for a head-plus-tail guess.
---
 python/freetoken/engine/engine.py       |  2 +-
 python/freetoken/scheduler/scheduler.py | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/python/freetoken/engine/engine.py b/python/freetoken/engine/engine.py
index c2fef43..bef13bd 100644
--- a/python/freetoken/engine/engine.py
+++ b/python/freetoken/engine/engine.py
@@ -630,7 +630,7 @@ class Engine:
             self._resolve_hybrid_fetch(config, cache)
         # Must be set before CUDA graph capture so the (device-side) accumulation ops are
         # captured and re-run on every decode replay.
-        cache.collect_stats = config.moe_collect_stats
+        cache.collect_stats = config.moe_collect_stats or os.environ.get("FREETOKEN_MOE_STATS", "0") == "1"
         # attach_offload_moe_cache walks for OffloadMoELayers, or defers to a model's
         # _iter_offload_moe_layers() hook when its MoE blocks are bespoke nn.Modules (DSV4).
         layers = attach_offload_moe_cache(self.model, cache)
diff --git a/python/freetoken/scheduler/scheduler.py b/python/freetoken/scheduler/scheduler.py
index 662dc33..d9f8b75 100644
--- a/python/freetoken/scheduler/scheduler.py
+++ b/python/freetoken/scheduler/scheduler.py
@@ -320,6 +320,22 @@ class Scheduler(SchedulerIOMixin):
     def _process_last_data(self, last_data: ForwardData | None) -> None:
         if last_data is None:
             return
+        # diagnostic: cumulative per-layer decode miss stats every 250 steps (FREETOKEN_MOE_STATS=1)
+        try:
+            _c = getattr(self.engine, "moe_offload_cache", None)
+            if _c is not None and getattr(_c, "collect_stats", False):
+                self._msd = getattr(self, "_msd", 0) + 1
+                if self._msd % 250 == 0:
+                    import json as _json
+                    _pl = _c.decode_miss_stats_per_layer()["per_layer"]
+                    try:
+                        from freetoken.models.glm5_next.moe import offload_moe_layers
+                        _map = offload_moe_layers(self.engine.model.config)
+                    except Exception:
+                        _map = None
+                    logger.info_rank0("[moe-stats] " + _json.dumps({"bank_to_layer": _map, "per_layer": [{k: (round(v, 3) if isinstance(v, float) else v) for k, v in d.items()} for d in _pl]}))
+        except Exception as _e:
+            logger.warning(f"[moe-stats] dump failed: {_e!r}")
 
         batch, (_, next_tokens_cpu, copy_done) = last_data[0].batch, last_data[1]
         copy_done.synchronize()
